/**
 * @t4r71/dsh-guard — the two degeneration guards, merged, plus automatic retry.
 *
 * ## What this package is
 *
 * `@t4r71/dsh-stream-guard` and `@t4r71/dsh-idle-guard` were two plugins that
 * watched the same boundary and did not know about each other. Mounted
 * together they could inject two messages for one failure: a brake on the way
 * out of the stream, and a continuation when the steered turn then ended on
 * reasoning alone. Each message is a user turn in the transcript, so the
 * duplication was not free.
 *
 * This package is both of them, in one `apply`, sharing one per-session state
 * and one boundary token. Every trigger condition, every threshold and every
 * budget is the one the source package shipped — the merge removes duplicate
 * injection, it does not re-tune anything.
 *
 * ## The three seams it uses
 *
 * - `llm/stream` (**waterfall**) — the brake. The listener must *return* the
 *   stream object; returning nothing swallows it.
 * - `agent/turn-stopping` (**serial**, payload `{agent, turn, signal}`) — the
 *   arbitration point. Steering here keeps the turn open, because the loop
 *   re-reads its inbox after this boundary and only then decides to break
 *   (`dsh-agent-loop/lib/index.js:983-990`).
 * - `agent/request-error` (**waterfall**) — the automatic-retry fallback.
 *   Returning `{kind:'retry'}` makes the loop re-run the same step
 *   (`dsh-agent-loop/lib/index.js:1109-1119`).
 *
 * All three are event seams, so this guard works with the stock
 * `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-pi-ai` access layer unchanged. It replaces nothing.
 *
 * ## Shared state
 *
 * One `SessionState` per session (both guards' counters, renamed apart where
 * they collided) and one `injected` map holding the boundary token
 * `turn:lastAssistantMessageId`. The first rule to claim a boundary injects;
 * every later rule on that same boundary is skipped. See the arbitration
 * listener at the bottom of this file.
 *
 * ## Automatic retry
 *
 * The shipped runtime already retries provider-request failures
 * (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-retry`, 5 attempts, 500 ms → 10 s backoff). This
 * package adds only the tier that is missing: a bounded, delayed fallback for
 * the failures that policy declines, and turn-level recovery for an empty or
 * reasoning-only turn, which is not a request failure at all. Details in
 * `src/retry.ts`; measurements in `M:/T4/out/guard/E-守卫插件.md`.
 *
 * @module @t4r71/dsh-guard
 */

